00:19:09.720 --> 00:19:10.620
Maybe next time.

00:19:15.730 --> 00:19:18.710
Inuit people have always lived in harmony with nature.

00:19:19.210 --> 00:19:22.710
Even today, they continue to do that when they feast on a seal.

00:19:23.290 --> 00:19:26.150
Nothing's wasted, and if something cannot be eaten,

00:19:26.730 --> 00:19:29.130
the Inuit will find a way to get the best out of it.

00:19:30.000 --> 00:19:33.780
taken clothes out of sealskin, or jewelry with its bones.

00:19:33.940 --> 00:19:35.640
This here is the kidney.

00:19:36.560 --> 00:19:37.200
The kidney?

00:19:37.500 --> 00:19:37.740
Yeah.

00:19:38.250 --> 00:19:38.930
It's delicious.

00:19:39.540 --> 00:19:40.020
Yeah.

00:19:40.340 --> 00:19:42.830
Well, I think I'm going to stick to this part.

00:19:46.060 --> 00:19:46.480
Tasty?

00:19:47.730 --> 00:19:50.020
Well, it depends on what your taste is.

00:19:52.110 --> 00:19:52.590
Ugh.

00:19:53.030 --> 00:19:57.180
Well, it seems like I have a lot of energy, so I think I'm going to stop eating.

00:19:57.930 --> 00:19:58.410
Okay.

00:19:58.710 --> 00:19:59.590
I'll continue.

00:20:00.000 --> 00:20:00.220
OK.

00:20:02.520 --> 00:20:07.420
What happens to you in extreme cold weather?

00:20:07.620 --> 00:20:10.560
Let's pretend nicks and ticks are at the South Pole.

00:20:10.960 --> 00:20:13.080
And it was freezing outside.

00:20:13.430 --> 00:20:16.470
If you were naked, you would be dead in about 20 minutes

00:20:16.470 --> 00:20:17.530
from hypothermia.

00:20:18.010 --> 00:20:18.530
I'm nuts.

00:20:18.800 --> 00:20:21.890
But actually, it's much colder in this part of the world.

00:20:22.050 --> 00:20:23.430
So let's make it colder.

00:20:23.880 --> 00:20:25.220
Mine is 40 degrees.

00:20:25.520 --> 00:20:28.500
This is about three times as cold as your kitchen freezer.

00:20:28.800 --> 00:20:29.780
At this temperature.

00:20:30.120 --> 00:20:32.040
you'd be able to hear your breath freeze.

00:20:32.360 --> 00:20:34.780
Your nostrils would freeze shut when you inhale.

00:20:35.080 --> 00:20:38.620
And if your eyes became misty, your eyelids would freeze shut.

00:20:39.070 --> 00:20:41.730
But let's make it about minus 50 degrees.

00:20:41.990 --> 00:20:44.270
That's the average temperature in Antarctica,

00:20:44.510 --> 00:20:45.950
the coldest place on Earth.

00:20:46.320 --> 00:20:48.500
Your teeth will crack if exposed,

00:20:48.890 --> 00:20:51.930
and any bare skin will freeze within seconds,

00:20:51.950 --> 00:20:53.030
causing frostbite.

00:20:53.500 --> 00:20:56.280
At this temperature, hot water thrown into the air

00:20:56.280 --> 00:20:58.200
will freeze before it hits the ground.

00:21:00.670 --> 00:21:09.110
The coldest temperature ever recorded on Earth is minus 89 degrees Celsius or minus 130 degrees Fahrenheit in Antarctica.

00:21:09.830 --> 00:21:19.720
NASA tests some of its spacecraft there to see how they would work on a planet like Mars, which is as cold as Antarctica.

00:21:30.250 --> 00:21:30.510
Hello?

00:21:31.020 --> 00:21:32.080
Hey Tyler, it's Alicia.

00:21:32.900 --> 00:21:33.940
Modern technology.

00:21:34.340 --> 00:21:35.680
Hi Alicia, how's the Arctic?

00:21:36.240 --> 00:21:37.000
You should be here.

00:21:37.140 --> 00:21:38.000
It's so cool.

00:21:38.620 --> 00:21:39.700
Of course it's cool.

00:21:40.110 --> 00:21:41.550
After all, it is the Arctic.

00:21:42.320 --> 00:21:44.300
So, I hear you made a house out of snow.

00:21:45.360 --> 00:21:47.340
I guess there's no place like home.

00:21:47.500 --> 00:21:48.340
You're so funny.

00:21:49.580 --> 00:21:50.680
So, did you get me a souvenir?

00:21:51.060 --> 00:21:52.580
I'm emailing it to you right now.

00:21:53.300 --> 00:21:54.980
You're emailing me a souvenir?

00:21:55.500 --> 00:21:56.740
Yeah, it's an SB file.

00:21:57.160 --> 00:21:58.420
I'll open it.

00:21:58.540 --> 00:21:59.000
SB?

00:21:59.550 --> 00:21:59.970
What is it?

00:22:00.060 --> 00:22:00.800
What does the B stand for?

00:22:02.980 --> 00:22:03.540
Snowball.

00:22:04.360 --> 00:22:05.320
I did it!
